course: dictionary
lesson: 10132
title: Threaten: warning or danger
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To threaten someone is to say you will hurt them, or do something bad, if they do not do what you want. «The King keeps threatening to have him executed.» The King is warning the man that something terrible will happen unless he obeys.
explain: Something can also threaten a thing just by being a danger to it. «Early-winter ice can be thin, and falling through it is life-threatening.» The ice does not speak, but it is dangerous, so it threatens people.
explain: Threaten can also mean that something bad seems likely to happen soon. «It threatens to rain» means the sky looks like rain is coming. Read the words around threaten to find which meaning fits.
fact: Threaten is a verb: threaten, threatens, threatened, threatening.
fact: «Threatened» can mean in danger, as in a threatened species: an animal or plant that might die out.
fact: A threatening look makes you feel afraid or uneasy.
fact: When threatened, a fire-bellied toad arches its back to show its bright belly. This is a warning that its skin makes bad-tasting slime.
fact: If someone threatens you, online or in person, tell a trusted adult straight away.
exercise: «The King keeps threatening to have him executed.» What does threatening mean here? | Singing a happy song to someone | Giving someone a present | *Saying he will hurt or punish someone unless they obey | Forgetting someone's name
exercise: A threatened species is one that is in danger. What does threatened mean here? | *In danger of dying out | Kept safe in a zoo | Newly born | Very fast and strong
exercise: «It threatens to rain» means what? | The rain is warm | It is very hot and sunny | The rain has stopped | *Rain looks likely soon
test: «Early-winter ice can be thin, and falling through it is life-threatening.» What does life-threatening mean? | Very cold and fun | *Dangerous enough to cause death | Hard to see in the snow | Good for skating
test: Someone threatens you online. What should you do? | *Tell a trusted adult straight away | Reply with a bigger threat | Wait a week to see what happens | Ignore it and hope it stops
exam: Which sentence uses threaten to mean that something bad seems likely soon? | Dark clouds are a kind of cake | *Dark clouds threaten rain | Dark clouds have gone away | Dark clouds shine like silver
